<title>BELGIUM: BELGIAN RECTICEL TO SKIP DIVIDEND AGAIN.</title>
<headline>BELGIAN RECTICEL TO SKIP DIVIDEND AGAIN.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Recticel SA , a Belgian producer of polyurethane foam products, said on Wednesday it would not pay a dividend on 1996 earnings.</p>
<p>The group, 70-percent owned by Belgian holding company Societe Generale de Belgique SA (SGB) , did not pay a dividend on 1995 earnings either.  </p>
<p>Recticel's 1996 loss narrowed to 38 million francs, from 682 million in 1995.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
